      "settings": {
        "text_width": "wide",
        "title": "Why Choose Joysway Racing Yachts?",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Precision and Performance</strong>: Experience unmatched sailing with models designed for optimal performance and precision handling.</li><li><strong>Innovative Design</strong>: Each <a href=\"https://www.hearnshobbies.com/collections/joysway-rc-boats\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">Joysway racing yacht and boat</span></a> boasts a sleek, aerodynamic design, ensuring a smooth sailing experience.</li><li><strong>Durable Construction</strong>: Built to last, Joysway Racing Yachts are made with high-quality materials that withstand the elements.</li></ul>",
        "button_text": "",
        "button_link": ""
      }
    },
    "811a8acc-6441-464f-b4a9-e47fdf023532": {
      "type": "offers",
      "blocks": {
        "template--16341167472801__811a8acc-6441-464f-b4a9-e47fdf023532-offer-1": {
          "type": "offer",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Dragon Force 65 (DF65)",
            "content": "<p>The DF65, a smaller counterpart to the DF95, boasts a combination of high performance and accessibility, making it a top choice for both beginners and experienced RC sailors. Here are some key aspects:</p><ul><li><strong>Design and Build: </strong>The DF65 features an ABS hull, profiled aluminum fin, and molded plastic rudder. It is based on the ICE design and has undergone significant transformations over its versions to improve quality and performance. Notable features include a carbon fiber mast and boom tubes, an extruded aluminum keel with a zinc alloy ballast bulb, and a metal-geared digital rudder servo.</li><li><strong>Sails and Rigging:</strong> It comes with 50-micron Mylar film racing sails with printed flow stripes and logo. The rig is a full-sized, fractional low-aspect rig with carbon spars and a ball-raced gooseneck, contributing to its top-tier performance.</li><li><strong>Specifications:</strong> The DF65 measures 650 mm in length, with a beam of 116.5 mm and an overall height of 1338 mm. Its sail area totals 2226 cm², divided between the mainsail (1460 cm²) and the jib (766 cm²). The total weight is around 1200g without batteries.</li><li><strong>Versions: </strong>The DF65 is available in Ready-To-Race (RTR) and Almost-Ready-To-Race (ARTR) versions. The RTR version includes a 2.4G 4CH digital proportional transmitter and receiver, while the ARTR version comes without radio gear.</li></ul>"
          }
        },
        "template--16341167472801__811a8acc-6441-464f-b4a9-e47fdf023532-offer-2": {
          "type": "offer",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Dragon Force 95 (DF95)",
            "content": "<p>The DF95 is a larger and more advanced model, known for its superior design and performance capabilities. Key features include:</p><ul><li><strong>Design and Build: </strong>The DF95 features a molded plastic hull with a painted finish, a molded carbon fiber keel, and a metal-geared digital rudder servo. Its design focuses on light wind performance and stability in stronger winds.</li><li><strong>Sails and Rigging: </strong>It is equipped with 50-micron Mylar film racing sails and an advanced sail control system for precise handling. The rig's height is 1050 mm, contributing to its excellent performance.</li><li><strong>Specifications: </strong>The DF95 has a length of 950 mm, a width of 125 mm, and an overall height of 1470 mm. The sail area totals 3736 cm² (mainsail: 2314 cm², jib: 1422 cm²), and its total weight is around 2000g without batteries.</li><li><strong>Performance: </strong>The DF95's lightweight and narrow hull provides exceptional performance in light winds, and its sail plan and rigging are designed to maintain balance and control even in stronger winds.</li></ul>"
          }
        }
      },
